{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Will walk securely</b> — that he does not fear harm." "<b>And he who twists his paths</b> — he knows the good, he is known to others, that he twists his paths when he falls into evils, and the witness is 'will walk securely.'" "Another interpretation: 'will know' — from the root of וידע חולי."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra parses יודע as cognate with וידע חולי (Psalms 38:10?), i.e., from a root meaning to be sick/weak; the phrase is quoted in Hebrew as his lexical anchor."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:51.729720628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}